      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. More specifically:\n\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected only into the spawned child process\u0027s environment\n- The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n- This means a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent follows the same scoping model \u2014 it receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
